review:
[b]This is the FPS with most potential on the market right now.[/b]

[b]Pros:[/b]

- id Software has managed to incorporate modern FPS mechanics into the classic Quake formula. The game definitely feels like a different style of Quake, but it is still a familiar beast;

- Lovecraftian map design and lore;

- Visceral and fast paced gameplay unlike anything else in the market right now;

- There are upgrades and a store but only cosmetic (harmless) upgrades.

[b]Cons:[/b]

- The development team hasn't been able to consistently give the updates that the game desperately needs and this has led to a steady bleed out of players that stopped playing and are waiting for the definitive release once everything is (hopefully) fixed;

- Lack of a single player mode with bots and no support for the modding comunity. Currently the developer's mindset is of an e-sports online only monetized experience. [b]I hope id Software realizes what a huge mistake this is before the release date;[/b]

- Even though the loot boxes are cosmetic only, I'd rather pay for entire skins if I want to. Considering all the hatred and public disgust that the lootbox system has managed to garner recently, there is a chance that id Software completely removes them in favour of a different more [b]respectable[/b] system;

[b]Conclusion:[/b]

We know that additional game modes, maps and characters are going to be added in the future and that there is going to be a constant rebalance of each character that gets added to the roster. I also know that id Software knows how to and wants to craft an amazing game. But I can also see that it is being held hostage by the current market and gaming trends.

Thankfully there exists a dedicated core of gamers that see the [b]unrivaled potential[/b] of this title and who will never let Quake fade into obscurity. These players will continue to play the game until its glorious release date or until the bitter end if it eventually fails.

[b]This is the last bastion of the arena shooter style. If this one fails it's over. If you are sick of what a joke FPS games have become, please support this game! 

It may very well be the last true arena shooter that you play.[/b]
